{"step_index":69,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T11:33:14Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Updated walkthrough for Jharkhand Tourism website focusing exclusively on famous places with enhanced animations.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Walkthrough: Famous Destinations of Jharkhand (Elevated Edition)\n\nThe website has been refined to focus **EXCLUSIVELY ON FAMOUS PLACES** of Jharkhand with advanced, award-winning animations.\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 What Was Changed & Elevated\n\n1. **Exclusively Famous Destinations**:\n   - The dataset, navigation, sections, and interactive map now focus strictly on Jharkhand's iconic famous wonders:\n     - **Hundru Falls** (Ranchi) — 98m cascading wonder\n     - **Betla National Park** (Latehar) — Tigers, wild elephants & 16th-century Chero forts\n     - **Patratu Valley & Dam** (Ramgarh) — Serpentine hairpin roads & emerald reservoir\n     - **Parasnath Hill / Shikharji** (Giridih) — Highest peak in Jharkhand (1,365m)\n     - **Baba Baidyanath Dham** (Deoghar) — Ancient Jyotirlinga & Shakti Peeth\n     - **Jonha Falls (Gautamdhara)** (Ranchi) — Hanging valley falls\n     